<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Valencia</h1><p class="st-meta">1238 CE – 1707 CE · capital Valencia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A realm of the Crown of Aragon created by James I's conquest, famed for its rice and silk, its 15th-century golden age and its own laws.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a> conquered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/third-taifa-of-valencia">Third Taifa of Valencia</a> between 1232 and 1245, taking the city in 1238. He made it a separate kingdom with its own legal code, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/furs-of-valencia">Furs of Valencia</a>, rather than attaching it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-aragon">Aragon</a> or <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-catalonia">Catalonia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Catalan and Aragonese settlers lived alongside a large Muslim population that farmed the irrigated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huerta">huertas</a>, producing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a>. In the 15th century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> was the Crown's largest city, building the Silk Exchange and producing writers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ausias-march">Ausiàs March</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joanot-martorell">Joanot Martorell</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revolt-of-the-brotherhoods">Germanies</a> revolt of 1519-1523 and the expulsion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moriscos">Moriscos</a> in 1609 brought upheaval.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> backed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-habsburg">Habsburg</a> claimant in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>. After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ile-bourbon">Bourbon</a> victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-almansa">Almansa</a> in 1707, Philip V abolished its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">Furs</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nueva-planta-decrees">Nueva Planta decrees</a>, absorbing it into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bourbon-spain">Bourbon Spain</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-valencia.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Valencia" width="320" height="455"><figcaption>Image: Mutxamel · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Regne_valencia_1441.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1238 CE – 1707 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Valencia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>James I, Peter IV, Ferdinand II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity, Islam (Mudéjar)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Valencian Catalan, Andalusi Arabic, Castilian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Regne de València</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1472&amp;focus=kingdom-of-valencia" aria-label="Kingdom of Valencia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4671 764 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Valencia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4991 1020L4991 1020M4991 1020L4984 945M4991 1020L4909 989"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4991 1020h0M4984 945h0M4909 989h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4991 1020h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4991 1020h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Valencia. <a href="/atlas?year=1472&amp;focus=kingdom-of-valencia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
